      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5a9741718ec0a63065f13a2d",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Ah, I was going to submit this but good to see there's already a post about this. I recently found out that desktop users can use Shift+F1-F8 keys to trigger all the different animations VR users can do with their remotes(hands).\n\nI don't currently own a \"proper\" VR headset, all I have is my phone. So here's how I play: Phone attached to one of the phone vr headset things(and Riftcat) and a PS4 controller to move around and such... so.. the game runs under \"VR-mode\". \n\nAfter creating some neat face expressions and testing them in \"Non-VR/Desktop mode\" and mapping these expressions to the D-Pad on my controller I jump on \"VR-Mode\" with my phone.. only to find that the \"Shift+F\" Keys are disabled in \"VR-Mode\". I found this odd because seems like the rest of the keyboard works just fine.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-28T23:55:29.350Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since the new update to use hand gesture's on keyboard had got me thinking.\nIn desktop mode you are able to use the new hand gestures but when you launch the vr mode the keyboard input for gestures doesnt seem to work or is disabled.\nThis is troublesome if you wish to rebind keys on a controller to use hand gestures to create animation overrides if you do not have the motion controllers but you have a vr headset.\nSince in vr mode all other keyboard keys can be used, is it possible to enable hand gestures aswell?",
